-- title:
--   The evolved state $|\Psi(t)\rangle = e^{-i\mathcal Ht}|\Psi_{in}\rangle$ (18)
-- statement:
--   For real $\gamma$, $t$ and $m, N\in\mathbb N$, let $M$ be the matrix of $\mathcal H$ (14) in the basis (15) of the sector. The evolved state of Eq. (18) is
--
--   $$|\Psi(t)\rangle = e^{-i\mathcal H t}|\Psi_{in}\rangle = \sum_{q} \big(e^{-iMt}\, e_{(0,0)}\big)_q \;|\mathrm{sectorIndex}(q)\rangle ,$$
--
--   where $e_{(0,0)}$ is the coordinate vector of $|\Psi_{in}\rangle = |m,0,0,0,N\rangle = |\mathrm{sectorIndex}(0,0)\rangle$ and $e^{-iMt}$ is the matrix exponential.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathcal H$ is unbounded on the full Fock space, but the span of the sector states (15) is finite-dimensional, contains $|\Psi_{in}\rangle$, and is invariant under $\mathcal H$; on it the Schrödinger evolution $e^{-i\mathcal Ht} = \sum_p (-i\mathcal Ht)^p/p!$ is the matrix exponential of the compression. The definition is for every real $t$ and $\gamma$.
-- source:
--   Kempe, Simon, Weihs, Λ's, V's, and optimal cloning with stimulated emission, arXiv:quant-ph/0003025v1, Sec. II C, (18), p.5

import Definitions.Def_KempeCloning_hamSector

namespace KempeCloning

/-- **The evolved state `|Ψ(t)⟩ = e^{−iHt} |Ψ_in⟩` of (18).**
Kempe, Simon, Weihs, arXiv:quant-ph/0003025v1, Sec. II C, (18), p.5:
"|Ψ(t)⟩ = e^{−iHt}|Ψin⟩".

With `M = hamSector γ m N` the matrix of `H` on the sector (15), the coordinate vector of
`|Ψ(t)⟩` in the basis (15) is `e^{−iMt} e_{(0,0)}`, where `e_{(0,0)}` is the coordinate vector of
`|Ψ_in⟩ = |m, 0, 0, 0, N⟩ = |sectorIndex (0, 0)⟩`; the state is the corresponding superposition
`Σ_q (e^{−iMt} e_{(0,0)})_q |sectorIndex q⟩`.

**Formalization Note.** `e^{−iHt}` is the matrix exponential (`NormedSpace.exp`) of the
compression of `H` to the finite, `H`-invariant sector (15) containing `|Ψ_in⟩`; since the sector
is invariant (milestone `sector_invariant`), this is the Schrödinger evolution generated by (14),
`Σ_p (−iHt)^p/p! |Ψ_in⟩`. It is defined for every real `t` and every real `γ`. -/
noncomputable def evolve (γ : ℝ) (m N : ℕ) (t : ℝ) : FockVec :=
  ∑ q : Sector N,
    ((NormedSpace.exp ((-(Complex.I * (t : ℂ))) • hamSector γ m N)).mulVec
        (Pi.single (⟨(0, 0), by simp⟩ : Sector N) 1) q) •
      Finsupp.single (sectorIndex m N q) 1

end KempeCloning


